ustjoshn/pi-pstack/skills/how/references/explainer-prompt.md","offset":1,"limit":400}}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":965,"output":218,"cacheRead":23424,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":20,"totalTokens":24607,"cost":{"input":0.0038599999999999997,"output":0.00436,"cacheRead":0.0093696,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0175896,"totalFromProvider":false}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794070916855,"responseId":"resp_0d12944da4096875016aef5985959487d0915f86775b74b022","rawStopReason":"completed","durationMs":6725,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_38e288c31fb349fc9958822011299ab4|fc_0d12944da4096875016aef5988169087d08da62cb2afac65ab","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"ENOENT: no such file or directory, access '/var/folders/11/m_kwnqr97632l_cjt0mhytvh0000gn/T/pstack-sticky-rpc-ZAVtC1/01-PROMPT-MODE-STICKY-rpc-r1/home/.pi/agent/pstack/pstack-models.md'"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"durationMs":1,"timestamp":1794070923582},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3aa2c406f1554aca97051c37bfc35d37|fc_0d12944da4096875016aef598b58c487d080322b86fc56d7ca","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Explainer Prompt Template\n\nBuild the explainer subagent's prompt from this template. Fill in the placeholders.\n\n---\n\nYou are writing an architectural explanation for a senior engineer. Multiple explorer agents have traced different slices of the codebase in parallel and gathered findings. Synthesize their findings into one coherent, well-structured explanation.\n\n## Original Question\n\n> {QUESTION}\n\n## Explorer Findings\n\n{EXPLORER_FINDINGS_ALL}\n\n## Instructions\n\nThe explorers each investigated a different angle of the same subsystem. Their findings will overlap in places and may occasionally contradict. Reconcile them. Merge overlapping descriptions, resolve contradictions by checking the code yourself, and combine the separate slices into a unified picture.\n\nWrite an explanation a senior engineer unfamiliar with this area could read and walk away with a solid mental model, understanding the architecture well enough to start working in it confidently.\n\nYou have read-only access to the codebase to check anything, clarify a detail, or fill a gap. Use `read`, `grep`, and `find` as needed. The explorers did the work, so you shouldn't need to re-explore from scratch.\n\n## Output Format\n\nUse this structure, adapted to what makes sense for the question. Not every section is needed for every question.\n\n### Overview\n1-2 paragraphs. What is this thing, what does it do, why does it exist. Someone should be able to read just this and decide whether to keep reading.\n\n### Key Concepts\nThe important types, services, or abstractions needed to follow the rest. Brief definitions, not exhaustive.\n\n### How It Works\nThe core of the explanation, and the longest section. Walk through the flow: what triggers it, what happens step by step, where data goes, what the decision points are.\n\nUse prose, not pseudocode. Reference specific files and functions so the reader knows where to look, but don't dump large code blocks unless a snippet is essential to a point.\n\nWhen the flow involves multiple components talking to each other, or data transforming through stages, include a diagram. Use mermaid (```mermaid) for structured flows (sequence diagrams, flowcharts, component graphs) or ASCII art for simpler relationships where mermaid would be overkill. Use your judgment. A diagram should clarify, not decorate. If prose covers the flow, skip the diagram.\n\n### Where Things Live\nA brief file/directory map. Just the ones someone would need to start working here.\n\n### Gotchas\nNon-obvious things, surprising behavior, historical context, pitfalls. Skip this section if there's nothing worth calling out.\n\n## Communication Style\n\n- Use concrete language, not abstractions-about-abstractions\n- Say \"the `UserService` calls `AuthClient.refresh()`\" not \"the service delegates to the client\"\n- When something is complex, explain why it's complex. Don't just describe the complexity\n- When something is simple, don't pad it out\n- If there's a helpful analogy, use it. If there isn't, don't force one\n- If the explorers flagged open questions or gaps, acknowledge them rather than hiding them\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":1,"timestamp":1794070923583},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning model grok handling**\n\n**Defining task handling with poteto skill**","thinkingSignature":"{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"rs_0d12944da4096875016aef598ccf2487d08c2da303e7a490e6\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning model grok handling**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Defining task handling with poteto skill**\"}],\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABq71mQSd2f6rRyg1Rab1TvKpU9EfYYNPIaYxSQGZGa7nYMT9gV6FoYvIiB_1jCkayfdpNNtjQzOz0wcgD36yHT8J8Ec9OSdfPuNHQ1ka7tF235Z2t9lWYAo-YURO3rp7g8kzThbhgbG00VMdYgcmW7KQwj6gKHbY0x9wI3r0Ez6cOkbN3tq5Cp4fXh_psxs4zn6-k81mTrmTQgv7wjq-ijlBq8stLBUq6-lvJL7kY33j9RLQA5Ln_aEQDySlkmlat1yQ1k8zzqPaAjFKdVA-4aktfHV25hMKW_0FmZ0VvuxJdMSyT3KWGgNDDXyx6VLmLMcJ3LQv1UB_zRlRWin6ndvctB-MkEhjFICrmNZQgvMLP4yJVFF6pIvbVlOxk2-FzUY1lNElzRUttyf-h-e8BGZjwDjbMyXl-8Bjh44vX-LVKB2jsglX916PW_B8juzY844EDYWO81ANCTf-vGEhljj-ythZGZCUKafarQeA9GLDhokkQ3M9zkY3qEktwIqH9-GeY9QM21gjaDmXJb-a0a3ay4TaDimVgS41eh0jfleuVQ_LvWOwMreHVKRxGBWDu52UlTS7VvefcLWfNsSBrFxjVplSX3LEjB8EF61SWA7Y1CcsprOq4nbC1UWDZJ7SeU72cUNfKs0sX6zKgQxge-LmYVE0OZye2TzrEPrXnCwN1sE1vGiVMIsmz4ChTT6kQ8fwwM2715hdSTY7bUNLyzdTl6lK37EtVO72Cbe-5ecg8jqqFUY7est8ZZO_BENqM0URRZFSM22ZnyLQMOzxpvq-WU6GkYRRV0j2bb5fxqkvTukfKkq_GiMWMNrDH-9e3b2RW7KUp6DKbHXWsW3AKLbZBzJFRQM1-JgtQuC7f61cfu2PZ1zjQS7VAovVF98qHL8zQ6xrWOtUHRgu7JLfUDYovRfk5EE21DTnjAXkCAwA3IIWkQIXugrM11AJzWWLjtBVvUTCijIhIpNypbfGMNJgM6foAREmeasf6EugnEf87Ov32DEWjvy8SwDpWNllQDKm1YlztCKwa_B0njf0LH7AKDDLEtMT1LC039nQ4AYjeenzGA9jO0I8lUblFkVNlFLw2ECobypFIk6GiWhKx